Guidelines for Water Reuse — EPA and USAID, 2012 (@wu-reuse: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_5D8YEK23KH0G3994XRY2JA16PK
US Environmental Protection Agency and US Agency for International Development, with CDM Smith and contributing authors. EPA/600/R-12/618, September 2012. [Official text](https://nepis.epa.gov/Exe/ZyPURL.cgi?Dockey=P100FS7K.TXT) · [Complete PDF](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2019-08/documents/2012-guidelines-water-reuse.pdf).

Read the whole technical and case-study account progressively. Chapters 1–3 develop purposes, system planning and applications; section 3.5 focuses on industrial uses. Compare treatment, monitoring and project evidence in later chapters with a specific proposed use. Read historical regulatory summaries in their dated context and retrieve applicable current requirements separately.

The agency text, contents and selected industrial/reliability sections were inspected on 30 October 2026. Public reading is authorized; preserve contributor, photograph and other component notices. The book describes guidance and examples rather than supplying a universal reuse specification. References and individual case studies are starting points for further primary investigation.

